## 4. Data quality rules the feature relies on

| Rule | Why | What the POC does today |
|---|---|---|
| Every held security maps to a CMA asset class | Unclassified value is left out of the math | Shows coverage and lists unclassified holdings |
| Every lot has an adjusted cost basis and an acquisition date | Tax and term | Lots without basis are not sold; missing dates are treated as long-term and flagged |
| Look-through is no older than one quarter | Concentration through funds | Shows the look-through date |
| Investment profile and target are reviewed within 12â36 months (house rule) | Alignment is only as good as the profile | Not checked |
| Tax bracket and state on file for taxable accounts | Tax figures | Assumes 37% and no state rate, and lists that as unresolved |
| Manager-run positions identified at sleeve level | The advisor must not be told to trade them | Uses sleeve records |
| Research ratings are entitled to the user | Compliance | Not modeled |
| One as-of date per run, shown on screen | Reproducible answers | Positions, look-through and research dates shown |

